ion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 45%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 41.0 vs 18.7 and EV/EBITDA 15.3 vs 11.0 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 16% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of -4.0% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 1.5% (vs the 8% bar).","The 10 covering analysts target $18.90 on average, 49% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 3% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.8%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.42).","It burns cash (FCF margin -3%).","ROE of 3% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.8x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.9% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.4x net debt to EBITDA ($21.2M of cash against $269.1M of debt), above the 1.5x gate, and interest cover is thin at 1.6x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.07 in the distress zone.","The current ratio of 0.29 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 18.7% over 3 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 3.4% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 21%.","Capex runs 2.1x depreciation (12.8% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.8%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (13 sales, net $3.0M sold).","The share count has grown 0.9% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","Short interest is elevated at 10.8% of the float, 3.0 days to cover."],"people":["With about 19,000 employees, each generates about $64K of revenue, 0.2x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 19.4% a year across its filed history.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$2K per employee.","CEO pay is $1.9M (30x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (10/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"score":27.5,"head":"Red flag: priced 449% above its fair value of $2.31.","pros":["Revenue grew 18.7%/yr over 3y","10 analysts' mean target $18.90 (+49%)"],"cons":["Trades 449% above fair value of $2.31","ROIC 3.4% vs WACC 8.8%","FCF margin 2.5% (burns cash)","Interest coverage only 1.6x","Altman Z in the distress zone (1.07)"],"flags":["Priced 449% above its fair value of $2.31","Altman Z in the distress zone (1.07)","Earns below its cost of capital and burns cash"],"vc":{"base":2.31,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":2.31,"n_alt":2,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.4529,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (45% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":18.6799,"ev_ebitda":11.018,"pfcf":16.4777,"pb":2.2768,"roic":0.1253,"gross_margin":0.346,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0226}},"ticker":"FWRG","date":"2026-11-27"}